  "power_note": "The classical panel is enough to estimate a within-player rating gradient and a year term, and still not enough to add career curvature on top: that spec's year interval is several times wider and its curvature term does not exclude zero. Enlarging the panel did not fix it, because the limit is collinearity rather than sample size, which is the standard age-period-cohort result (Fosse & Winship 2019).",
